WEBVTT

legitimacy-02-1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:06.411
Previously: nation, state, and
sovereignty—three pillars vouching for

legitimacy-02-2
00:00:06.411 --> 00:00:07.300
one another.

legitimacy-02-3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:14.540
This time: how is a “we” made on a
production line?

legitimacy-02-4
00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:20.440
Episode 2: The Legitimacy Production Line

legitimacy-02-5
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.843
Imagine her returning home today after
six months away on business. From leaving

legitimacy-02-6
00:00:26.843 --> 00:00:29.770
the plane to exiting the airport takes
about twenty minutes.

legitimacy-02-7
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:35.728
Those twenty minutes take her through a
whole legitimacy production line. Five

legitimacy-02-8
00:00:35.728 --> 00:00:36.950
stations in all.

legitimacy-02-9
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.210
Station one: a wall. “Welcome back to
Country X.”

legitimacy-02-10
00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:48.245
It checks no one. It simply declares,
first: this land belongs to “us,” and

legitimacy-02-11
00:00:48.245 --> 00:00:49.130
always has.

legitimacy-02-12
00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:54.460
① Sovereignty myth: first, declare “This
place is ours.”

legitimacy-02-13
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.180
Station two: two signs.

legitimacy-02-14
00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.170
No one has checked her documents yet, but
the queues have already divided people

legitimacy-02-15
00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.480
into “us” and “them.”

legitimacy-02-16
00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.900
② Us/the Other: classify first.

legitimacy-02-17
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:14.354
Guess what comes next: once the queues
are divided, what makes that

legitimacy-02-18
00:01:14.354 --> 00:01:17.340
classification “keep counting”?

legitimacy-02-19
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:22.660
The answer: write it down. Station three,
the counter.

legitimacy-02-20
00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.147
“Under Article X of national law,
citizens have the right to enter.” The

legitimacy-02-21
00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:30.200
sign from earlier becomes a legal
provision here.

legitimacy-02-22
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:35.007
③ Legal provisions: write the
classification into law, making it seem

legitimacy-02-23
00:01:35.007 --> 00:01:36.400
“the natural order.”

legitimacy-02-24
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.320
Station four: a facial recognition gate.

legitimacy-02-25
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.779
Cameras, databases, entry and exit
records. The state need not know her

legitimacy-02-26
00:01:45.779 --> 00:01:48.480
personally to “see” who she is in a
second.

legitimacy-02-27
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.420
④ Technical identification: let the state
“see” everyone clearly.

legitimacy-02-28
00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.624
Scott, Seeing Like a State (1998): to
govern, the state must first make

legitimacy-02-29
00:01:55.624 --> 00:01:57.610
populations and land “legible.”
(Paraphrase)

legitimacy-02-30
00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.340
“I'm back.”

legitimacy-02-31
00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:05.061
Station five: everything runs smoothly,
safely, and in order. She breathes a sigh

legitimacy-02-32
00:02:05.061 --> 00:02:05.520
of relief.

legitimacy-02-33
00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:12.049
⑤ Realized legitimacy: the results of
governance make it all feel as it should

legitimacy-02-34
00:02:12.049 --> 00:02:12.300
be.

legitimacy-02-35
00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.541
That smooth experience then proves, in
turn, that the wall, the two queues, the

legitimacy-02-36
00:02:17.541 --> 00:02:19.730
law, and the gate were all right.

legitimacy-02-37
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:23.077
Author's thesis §2.3: governance outcomes
“retroactively” legitimate the first four

legitimacy-02-38
00:02:23.077 --> 00:02:24.690
stages; failure weakens the whole chain.

legitimacy-02-39
00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:32.260
In another lane, the gate turns red. He
is asked to step aside: “Please wait.”

legitimacy-02-40
00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:37.240
When everything runs smoothly, no one
thinks of it as a “production line.”

legitimacy-02-41
00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:42.700
Only those who get stuck can see every
station.

legitimacy-02-42
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.640
This episode's reference card (take a
screenshot)

legitimacy-02-43
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.360
① Sovereignty myth | The wall at arrivals
| First declares: “This place is ours.”

legitimacy-02-44
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.770
② Us/the Other | Two queue signs |
Classify first.

legitimacy-02-45
00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.556
③ Legal provisions | The counter and
legal text | Write the classification as

legitimacy-02-46
00:02:55.556 --> 00:02:56.280
“the natural order.”

legitimacy-02-47
00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.145
④ Technical identification | Facial
recognition gates and databases | Let the

legitimacy-02-48
00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:00.150
state see everyone clearly.

legitimacy-02-49
00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:06.798
⑤ Realized legitimacy | “I'm back” |
Outcomes validate the first four stations

legitimacy-02-50
00:03:06.798 --> 00:03:07.480
in turn.

legitimacy-02-51
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.590
Legitimacy is not made once and for all.

legitimacy-02-52
00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:19.025
It must be produced again at every
entrance, on every form, and with every

legitimacy-02-53
00:03:19.025 --> 00:03:20.030
face scan.

legitimacy-02-54
00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.690
Next episode:

legitimacy-02-55
00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:27.840
No “us” without “them”?

legitimacy-02-56
00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:35.050
This is UjiBricks.
